    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d415">

                <pb facs="d415-01" n="1" xml:id="d415-01"/>

                <head>415. Telegram 56144 From the Department of State to
                    the Embassy in Pakistan<anchor n="1" xml:id="d415-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d415-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1972-04-01T00:48:00+00:00">April 1, 1972, 0048Z</date>
                </dateline>
                <list type="references">
                    <head>REF:</head>
                    <item>Islamabad 1675</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT:</label>
                    <item>Timing of Bangladesh Recognition</item>
                </list>
                <p>1. You should inform President Bhutto
                    soonest that we have reviewed entire matter of Bangladesh recognition, giving
                    careful consideration to his suggestions on timing. We have concluded we should
                    recognize in near future and want Bhutto
                    to know that we plan to announce recognition on April 4. You should caution him
                    that this information must be held in closest confidence until our announcement
                    made.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d415-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d415-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Files
                    1970–73, POL 16 BANGLADESH. Secret; Priority;
                    Nodis. Drafted by Laingen; cleared by
                        Davies, Sisco, Brown, and Kissinger; and approved by Rogers. Repeated Priority to Dacca and New Delhi</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d415-f2" n="2" xml:id="d415-f2-content">
                <p>Chargé Sober was instructed to inform Pakistani President Bhutto that the United States intended to
                    recognize Bangladesh on April 4.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
